WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.994
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:06.487 --> 00:00:09.300
There's a new Black Panther
with a new look in Marvel

00:00:09.300 --> 00:00:10.410
Studios' "Black Panther--

00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:11.400
Wakanda Forever."

00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:13.320
So to get the scoop
on the suit, I'm

00:00:13.320 --> 00:00:16.090
talking with Marvel Studios
head of visual development Ryan

00:00:16.090 --> 00:00:17.355
Meinerding.
Hi, Ryan.

00:00:17.355 --> 00:00:18.270
Hello.

00:00:18.270 --> 00:00:20.010
Well, let's jump in.

00:00:20.010 --> 00:00:22.890
Shuri's new Black Panther
suit is an incredible take

00:00:22.890 --> 00:00:26.350
on an already iconic suit, so as
you started work on this film,

00:00:26.350 --> 00:00:27.735
how did you approach
this new design?

00:00:27.735 --> 00:00:29.550
RYAN MEINERDING: One of the
great things about Shuri

00:00:29.550 --> 00:00:31.950
in the first "Black Panther"
movie was that she had, like,

00:00:31.950 --> 00:00:35.190
pretty amazing iconic
looks across the board,

00:00:35.190 --> 00:00:36.660
some that Ruth
Carter designed, some

00:00:36.660 --> 00:00:38.550
that the visual
development team designed.

00:00:38.550 --> 00:00:40.440
We were trying to
look at pretty early

00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:42.540
on with how to translate
some of those things

00:00:42.540 --> 00:00:43.950
into the Black Panther suit.

00:00:43.950 --> 00:00:46.860
And I think with Shuri, we
were trying to find almost

00:00:46.860 --> 00:00:48.480
a slightly more fierce look.

00:00:48.480 --> 00:00:50.970
I think we were trying to
evolve her into a character

00:00:50.970 --> 00:00:53.850
where she was stepping into
the mantle in a way that was

00:00:53.850 --> 00:00:56.250
tremendously her own
and that involved

00:00:56.250 --> 00:00:59.430
becoming a sort of more fierce
version of Black Panther.

00:00:59.430 --> 00:01:01.050
It's such an awesome design.

00:01:01.050 --> 00:01:03.660
What were some of the key
visual elements you and the team

00:01:03.660 --> 00:01:04.830
were looking to incorporate?

00:01:04.830 --> 00:01:07.740
In terms of the overall
aesthetic of the suit,

00:01:07.740 --> 00:01:09.480
it's kind of the same
as the other Panther

00:01:09.480 --> 00:01:12.720
suits where we're trying to
make it as skintight to her body

00:01:12.720 --> 00:01:14.490
as possible so it
feels flexible.

00:01:14.490 --> 00:01:16.110
It feels like she
can be acrobatic.

00:01:16.110 --> 00:01:17.800
She can be strong and powerful.

00:01:17.800 --> 00:01:20.517
It doesn't have to have any sort
of restrictions on her at all.

00:01:20.517 --> 00:01:22.350
You know, one of the things
that Ryan Coogler had asked

00:01:22.350 --> 00:01:25.440
for is sort of maybe even
weaponry or, you know,

00:01:25.440 --> 00:01:28.410
starting with her Panther
gauntlets becoming even larger

00:01:28.410 --> 00:01:31.710
or because she is, you know,
obviously a technology expert,

00:01:31.710 --> 00:01:35.100
the tech became added on
and those things got bulkier

00:01:35.100 --> 00:01:37.260
and almost made
the suit look more

00:01:37.260 --> 00:01:38.970
powerful through
having technology

00:01:38.970 --> 00:01:40.950
as part of a visual language.

00:01:40.950 --> 00:01:42.660
But as we got into
it we did realize

00:01:42.660 --> 00:01:45.180
we had so many amazing visual
reference points from Shuri

00:01:45.180 --> 00:01:47.820
in the previous movie that
we were kind of hearkening

00:01:47.820 --> 00:01:48.970
back to those a lot.

00:01:48.970 --> 00:01:50.370
I think the biggest
sort of change

00:01:50.370 --> 00:01:51.795
in the suit in the
previous designs

00:01:51.795 --> 00:01:54.870
is fundamentally the boldness
of the design language

00:01:54.870 --> 00:01:57.810
as well as the Panther gauntlets
and a few pieces of gold

00:01:57.810 --> 00:02:00.000
around her shoulders that
are a little bit stronger

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:01.560
and meant to give
her a little bit more

00:02:01.560 --> 00:02:03.150
of a shoulder
silhouette than she

00:02:03.150 --> 00:02:04.395
would have had without them.

00:02:04.395 --> 00:02:07.530
Well, you packed so many
amazing details into this suit.

00:02:07.530 --> 00:02:09.630
How many iterations
of Shuri's suit

00:02:09.630 --> 00:02:12.180
did the team create before
settling on the final design?

00:02:12.180 --> 00:02:15.340
We probably had 50 or
60 different designs.

00:02:15.340 --> 00:02:17.400
I think there was a lot
of really amazing things

00:02:17.400 --> 00:02:20.430
to play with, and having
the comics as a base

00:02:20.430 --> 00:02:22.380
but also having those
amazing appearances

00:02:22.380 --> 00:02:23.760
in the first movie
as a place to start

00:02:23.760 --> 00:02:25.770
was basically where we began.

00:02:25.770 --> 00:02:27.570
I think we ended up
landing on one that

00:02:27.570 --> 00:02:30.540
had that sort of fierce look
with things that represented

00:02:30.540 --> 00:02:33.420
Panther teeth both on the
top and bottom of her jaw

00:02:33.420 --> 00:02:35.820
and specifically
pulling from her warrior

00:02:35.820 --> 00:02:39.750
falls look where she had
a number of white dots

00:02:39.750 --> 00:02:40.950
painted on her face.

00:02:40.950 --> 00:02:43.800
We were trying to turn those
into sort of graphic elements

00:02:43.800 --> 00:02:47.100
that are done in silver, and
then finding all those things

00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:49.650
integrated into
one cohesive look

00:02:49.650 --> 00:02:52.090
was one of the more fun
parts of the process.

00:02:52.090 --> 00:02:54.930
And, again, bringing that
gold and silver in to sort of

00:02:54.930 --> 00:02:56.700
say that she's now at
a place where she's

00:02:56.700 --> 00:02:59.250
stepping into the
mantle, taking on all

00:02:59.250 --> 00:03:01.590
of the burden of where
her country is at

00:03:01.590 --> 00:03:03.150
and trying to save the day.

00:03:03.150 --> 00:03:05.940
Now, of course, Shuri
isn't the first person

00:03:05.940 --> 00:03:08.460
we've seen take on the
mantle of the Black Panther.

00:03:08.460 --> 00:03:10.650
Are there any parts
of this design

00:03:10.650 --> 00:03:12.870
that referenced previous
Black Panther suits?

00:03:12.870 --> 00:03:15.270
One of the fun things about
Marvel Studios and Marvel

00:03:15.270 --> 00:03:16.950
comics is that there
are characters that

00:03:16.950 --> 00:03:18.750
have these sort of mantles
that can get passed

00:03:18.750 --> 00:03:19.980
from one character to another.

00:03:19.980 --> 00:03:22.410
That symbol of
that mantle becomes

00:03:22.410 --> 00:03:24.840
different and changed in some
way when the new character

00:03:24.840 --> 00:03:25.680
takes it over.

00:03:25.680 --> 00:03:28.290
The suits that we start with
end up meaning something,

00:03:28.290 --> 00:03:30.810
and then how they translate into
the next film and the next film

00:03:30.810 --> 00:03:33.080
all seem to like become useful
in the storytelling going

00:03:33.080 --> 00:03:33.880
forward.

00:03:33.880 --> 00:03:36.210
And when we were working on the
Black Panther suit for "Civil

00:03:36.210 --> 00:03:38.520
War," that ended
up being sort of

00:03:38.520 --> 00:03:40.270
termed sort of T'Challa's suit.

00:03:40.270 --> 00:03:42.780
I think in the "Black Panther"
movie where T'Challa explains

00:03:42.780 --> 00:03:44.760
to Shuri that was
what he had developed,

00:03:44.760 --> 00:03:47.580
and Shuri creates that suit
in "Black Panther," right.

00:03:47.580 --> 00:03:49.890
And Killmonger ends up
taking that gold suit

00:03:49.890 --> 00:03:52.860
and sort of making it his
own at the end of that film.

00:03:52.860 --> 00:03:55.560
Essentially, the suit
that Shuri ends up with

00:03:55.560 --> 00:03:57.750
is kind of a combination
between T'Challa's

00:03:57.750 --> 00:04:00.840
suit and Killmonger's suit, a
mix of the silver and the gold.

00:04:00.840 --> 00:04:03.270
That's the Panther she needed
to become in order to be

00:04:03.270 --> 00:04:04.990
able to fight Namor at the end.

00:04:04.990 --> 00:04:07.620
There are some subtle nods
to each one of those suits

00:04:07.620 --> 00:04:08.910
in the final design,
but it really

00:04:08.910 --> 00:04:11.520
is as simple as the color
schemes being the silver

00:04:11.520 --> 00:04:13.210
and the gold being
the two things.

00:04:13.210 --> 00:04:16.620
There is a bit of through
line for her representing

00:04:16.620 --> 00:04:18.959
her fallen brother
as well as probably

00:04:18.959 --> 00:04:21.480
begrudgingly representing
things she needed

00:04:21.480 --> 00:04:23.010
to learn from Killmonger.

00:04:23.010 --> 00:04:25.440
So, Ryan, what
did it mean to you

00:04:25.440 --> 00:04:26.970
to be able to
continue the legacy

00:04:26.970 --> 00:04:30.330
of the Black Panther in the
MCU through a new character

00:04:30.330 --> 00:04:31.390
and this new design.

00:04:31.390 --> 00:04:32.490
RYAN MEINERDING:
The fact that we

00:04:32.490 --> 00:04:35.370
were able to work on
Shuri in "Black Panther"

00:04:35.370 --> 00:04:38.700
and to see her sort of
transition into a full on Black

00:04:38.700 --> 00:04:40.410
Panther of her own
in "Black Panther--

00:04:40.410 --> 00:04:42.600
Wakanda Forever," it was
an amazing experience.

00:04:42.600 --> 00:04:46.620
Like, the idea of watching
that character take on a mantle

00:04:46.620 --> 00:04:49.230
do things that she didn't think
she could do, try to live up

00:04:49.230 --> 00:04:51.900
to her brother's
memory, for me, it's

00:04:51.900 --> 00:04:54.510
to have been part of
this journey of watching

00:04:54.510 --> 00:04:57.840
this character become beloved
by the audience and the fans

00:04:57.840 --> 00:05:01.410
and trying to figure out how
Shuri can feel like she's

00:05:01.410 --> 00:05:03.710
taking that mantle and
carrying it forward

00:05:03.710 --> 00:05:04.830
was an incredible experience.

00:05:04.830 --> 00:05:09.205
I am the Black Panther,
and I'm here for retribution.

00:05:09.205 --> 00:05:11.380
Well, you and the
whole team really

00:05:11.380 --> 00:05:12.730
did an amazing job, Brian.

00:05:12.730 --> 00:05:14.240
Thank you so much
for talking with us.

00:05:14.240 --> 00:05:15.470
Thank you.
It was great to be here.

00:05:15.470 --> 00:05:16.270
Thank you so much.

00:05:16.270 --> 00:05:18.700
LANGSTON BELTON: And, of course,
everyone go experience Marvel

00:05:18.700 --> 00:05:19.840
Studios' "Black Panther--

00:05:19.840 --> 00:05:23.190
Wakanda Forever"
in theaters now.

